 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "n and m are positive integers and tasks a list of positive integer durations in minutes. The machines offer n * m slots that each run one task at a time, starting at minute 0. Tasks are started shortest first (equal durations in any order); each task goes to a slot that becomes free earliest and finishes at that free time plus its duration. A task is started only when it would finish at or before minute 60; once one task cannot fit, no longer task can. Return the number of tasks started.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
